            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"Spiritual purity, exclusive devotion, and faithfulness to God, most notably symbolizing the Church as the pure bride of Christ or faithful Israel.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"2 Corinthians 11:2\",\"Revelation 14:4\",\"Matthew 25:1-13\",\"Jeremiah 31:4\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"Literal celibacy or sexual purity as a high spiritual calling, heavily emphasized in early and medieval ascetic traditions.\",\"basis\":[\"1 Corinthians 7:25-34\",\"Matthew 19:12\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"A personified city or nation, often emphasizing vulnerability, inviolability, or tragedy (e.g., Virgin Daughter of Babylon, Virgin Israel).\",\"basis\":[\"Isaiah 47:1\",\"Amos 5:2\",\"Lamentations 2:13\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"Symbolically, the term is predominantly understood as representing the uncorrupted, faithful people of God (the Church or Israel) waiting for their bridegroom, distinguishing them from the spiritual adultery or idolatry seen in surrounding nations.\"}",
